 {"HEALTH_AND_SAFETY_WARNING_TITLE","Health And Safety Warning"},
 {"HEALTH_AND_SAFETY_WARNING_SHORT_VERSION","<align=center><size=120%>WARNING\r\n\r\nTHIS EXPERIENCE MAY CONTAIN FLASHING IMAGES THAT MAY TRIGGER SEIZURES IN PHOTOSENSITIVE INDIVIDUALS. SEE OCULUS.COM/WARNINGS.</size></align>"},
 {"HEALTH_AND_SAFETY_WARNING","<align=center><size=5>WARNING - THIS EXPERIENCE MAY CONTAIN FLASHING IMAGES</size></align>\r\n\r\nA small number of people may have seizures triggered by certain lights, patterns, or images, even with no history of seizures. Talk to a doctor first if you have an epileptic condition. Stop use if you experience any unusual symptoms and don’t resume until you have talked with a doctor. See oculus.com/warnings.\r\n\r\n<align=center><size=5>WARNING - THIS EXPERIENCE REQUIRES HIGH PHYSICAL ACTIVITY</size></align>\r\n\r\nAll users should read the health and safety warnings provided with your headset (and oculus.com/warnings) before playing.\r\nAlways create and maintain a safe play space. Take regular breaks. Stop if you experience discomfort.\r\n"},
 {"PS_HEALTH_AND_SAFETY_WARNING","<align=center><size=5>WARNING - THIS EXPERIENCE MAY CONTAIN FLASHING IMAGES</size></align>\r\n\r\nA small number of people may have seizures triggered by certain lights, patterns, or images, even with no history of seizures. Talk to a doctor first if you have an epileptic condition. Stop use if you experience any unusual symptoms and don’t resume until you have talked with a doctor.\r\n\r\n<align=center><size=5>WARNING - THIS EXPERIENCE REQUIRES HIGH PHYSICAL ACTIVITY</size></align>\r\n\r\nAll users should read the health and safety warnings provided with your headset before playing.\r\nAlways create and maintain a safe play space. Take regular breaks. Stop if you experience discomfort.\r\n"},
 {"HEALTH_AND_SAFETY_WARNING_CONTENT","A small percentage of people may experience seizures when exposed to certain lights, patterns or images even with no history of epilepsy or seizures.\r\n\r\nPlease read health and safety warnings in your VR headset instruction manual before playing Beat Saber. Because you may be encouraged to perform intense action with your controllers also make sure to review your surroundings and clear any obstacles in your play area before starting the game. Always remember to stay in the center of the cleared play area and do not walk around.\r\n\r\nPlaying Beat Saber requires high physical activity so follow the same habits as doing a regular workout. Don't forget to stretch before playing and rest regularly in between levels. Some people may experience muscle soreness. If you experience this then immediately stop playing the game and rest."},
